    [BugFix][KVPool] Fix MRV2 resume state and revert save suppression (#19693)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Port #19567 to main. MRV2 resumes preempted requests through
    `scheduled_new_reqs` with a full block table. AscendStore rebuilds the
    tracker but leaves `_preempted_req_ids` set. The next RUNNING step
    supplies a block delta and enters the preempted-request handler,
    replacing the full table and resetting save progress. This can cause
    `ReqMeta GVA metadata does not cover requested block range` or associate
    the wrong blocks with pool keys.
    
    Consume the marker in `_process_new_request` only when
    `use_v2_model_runner` is enabled. The root-cause fix is two lines.
    Revert #19534 (`c4f64438034a85ac68a93a788bbe1b2df84d6eb5`).
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: No new tests are added;
    existing UT and the reused lifecycle check cover the affected paths.
    - [x] **Regression test**: The lifecycle regression was rerun outside
    the PR; no new test file is committed.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: Runtime and NPU integration
    coverage remains for CI and hardware validation.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: No new tests are added.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: No hardware benchmark was run.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
